The solution is complete, verified, and stable. Final summary of the work:

## Deliverable

**`/workdir/solution.py`** + **`/workdir/implementation.c`** (single self-contained C file, ~2.1MB) + prebuilt **`implementation.so`** + `NOTES.md`.

## What was built

**Architecture per size** (all single-threaded AVX-512, no FFT libraries):
- **L=64** (new engine): CT(8×8) two-stage column codelets as small *rolled* loops in **digit-swapped storage order** — every stage-1 read and stage-2 write is a contiguous 8-slot group; 8×8 register-tile transposes fused inside the z-stages; the elementwise map fused between the completing stage-2 and next step's stage-1, with the map stage running as a **1-deep software pipeline** (map of group k overlaps the second DFT of group k−1 through a de-aliased staging buffer). One full-volume sweep per step by alternating slab (y,z) and pencil (x) visits, each completing step t and pre-transforming t+1; c pre-permuted into both consumption orders; rows padded to 136 doubles (4K-alias class), per-volume chains keep the active set ~13 MB.
- **L=45 / L=36** (new engines): same architecture with twiddle-free **PFA(5×9)/PFA(4×9)** stages in PFA-input-order storage (map fused at next stage-1's head; stage-2 writes via CRT position tables).
- **L=6, 8, 13, 17, 23** (+ batch-lane 36 for B≥8): the strongest prior-work engine (00291a90 final artifact), verified and routed per (L, B mod 8).

**Key machine findings that drove the design** (all re-measured): 2 FMA/cyc sustains with ≤2 loads+1 store per 8 FMAs; 1024-byte strides cause ~2.6× 4K-alias stalls; `rsqrt14/rcp14` are fast (1.3 tsc) — the microcode fear was context noise; software prefetch loses in every placement on this VM; hw sqrt/div maps lose on divider throughput; straight-line giant codelets lose to rolled loops.

## Results (this machine, pinned core, fresh processes)

- Workload proxy W3 (B=4, m=(25000,10000,3000,1200,800,500,400,300)) — validated against the graded scale by local MKL DFTI = **13.3 s**:
  - **this solution: best 2.199 s** (typical 2.20–2.25) ≈ **6× MKL**, ~10.5× the pocketfft base
  - best prior-work artifact on the same bench: 2.33 s
- **Correctness**: all 16 per-size gates pass at full-scale chain lengths (one-step ~8e-16 vs 1e-14 gate; worst m-step margin >12× under its gate), plus 19 randomized/edge shape cases (B=0/1/odd/16/40, m=1…13), bitwise-deterministic, no FFT-library symbols, links only libc/libm.

